        <briefdescription>
<para>Reads a table cell&apos;s raw text. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Reads <ref refid="namespaceId_1a3a978104a430eb23b80d82d88cd87664" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">Id::rawText</ref> directly, instead of through <ref refid="structjam_1_1MarkdownDocument_1a8ec1ddbed0a40a277e9201266a7a8a14" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">jam::ConfigDocument::getTableValue()</ref>, which resolves through getAllSubText(). Both cell-construction paths <ndash/> the markdown parser&apos;s addTableCell() and the in-memory addCell() <ndash/> write <ref refid="namespaceId_1a3a978104a430eb23b80d82d88cd87664" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">Id::rawText</ref> unconditionally, so every cell carries it as its exact source text. getAllSubText() instead walks a cell&apos;s rendered child elements, which addCell() never adds; reading <ref refid="namespaceId_1a3a978104a430eb23b80d82d88cd87664" kindref="member" external="/Users/jreng/Documents/Poems/dev/jam/docs/tagfile.xml">Id::rawText</ref> gives one reading that works for every manifest cell.</para>
